# Librem Blob Jail

This directory contains firmware/microcode needed for peripherals in some Librem boards, for OSes that do not provide device firmware.

When the blob jail feature is enabled, PureBoot provides device firmware to the OS by adding it to the initrd, then copying it to /run/firmware (see initrd/bin/inject_firmware.sh).

## Librem Mini v2

Librem Mini v2 currently ships with an Intel AX200, which requires the OS to provide firmware for both Wi-Fi and Bluetooth.

This model originally shipped an Atheros ath9k Wi-Fi/Bluetooth card, which does not require the OS to provide firmware for Wi-Fi (but does require it for Bluetooth).  These cards are no longer available, and the newer generations do require the OS to provide firmware.  Some whitelabeled Mini v2 devices shipped Intel AX200 earlier.

All PureBoot builds for Librem Mini v2 now include device firmware, and the firmware blob jail is activated by default if an Intel AX200 is installed.  The basic_usb_autoboot_blob_jail preconfiguration for Librem Mini v2 is now the same as basic_usb_autoboot as a result.

Firmware blob jail is still disabled by default on devices with Atheros ath9k cards, but it can be enabled for Bluetooth support.

## Librem 11

Librem 11 includes an Intel AX201 Wi-Fi/Bluetooth card, which requires the OS to provide firmware for both Wi-FI and Bluetooth.  All builds for librem_11 include the device firmware.

Display microcontroller firmware is also provided to enable power management.
